WEBVTT

00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:06.310
I see...

00:00:06.310 --> 00:00:09.820
So you came to Golonzo to learn about airships.

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:12.860
Do you want to be a skyfarer someday, Rackam?

00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:14.450
Yeah.

00:00:18.410 --> 00:00:21.120
I want to become a helmsman, see.

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:23.410
But that's not all.

00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:28.630
What I really plan to do
is fix the Grandcypher and help it fly!

00:00:30.590 --> 00:00:32.210
The Grandcypher...

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:35.430
To see the Grandcypher
soar through the skies again...

00:00:36.010 --> 00:00:37.600
That's my dream.

00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:45.600
But the thing is, everyone tells me
it's impossible or that I won't be able to fix it.

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:47.980
What do you think, Noa?

00:00:52.690 --> 00:00:54.990
I'm sure you can do it.

00:00:58.870 --> 00:01:02.490
I'll make the Grandcypher fly myself,
no matter what!

00:01:19.390 --> 00:01:21.260
Noa, that's amazing!

00:01:27.140 --> 00:01:28.100
Rackam...

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:33.190
I know you can make your dream come true.

00:01:35.610 --> 00:01:36.610
Yeah!

00:03:14.630 --> 00:03:19.300
I can't believe those jerks from the empire
made an attack while we weren't around...

00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:21.220
How low is that?

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:24.010
Lyria... Gran...

00:03:25.220 --> 00:03:29.770
Just look at what they did to the Grandcypher.
It's unforgivable!

00:03:30.940 --> 00:03:33.020
We'll go and rescue them immediately.

00:03:33.020 --> 00:03:38.730
Gran and Lyria were most likely taken
to the empire's garrison.

00:03:38.980 --> 00:03:41.860
Garrison? What's that?

00:03:41.860 --> 00:03:46.240
I heard they've been building some strange facilities.
It's probably one of them.

00:03:46.490 --> 00:03:52.410
It seems that some battleships
entered the adjoining port several days ago.

00:03:53.250 --> 00:03:54.080
Rackam.

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:55.420
Uh, right.

00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:58.300
What about Noa? Is he with them, too?

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:05.090
Apparently, there is a research lab in the garrison
for looking into using primal beasts and their powers.

00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:06.760
A lab?

00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:14.690
For years, the empire has been conducting
experiments on primal beasts in that lab.

00:04:14.690 --> 00:04:17.520
It's possible that they took Noa there.

00:04:49.930 --> 00:04:51.060
Rackam...

00:04:51.770 --> 00:04:54.600
If Gran and Lyria are taken off the island...

00:04:55.520 --> 00:04:59.940
If they use a small craft,
even the Grandcypher wouldn't be able to catch up.

00:05:00.690 --> 00:05:02.190
We have no time to lose.

00:05:02.440 --> 00:05:05.070
I'll be happy to join you!

00:05:05.070 --> 00:05:07.450
Really? Are you sure?

00:05:07.950 --> 00:05:11.910
Oh, you'll definitely be
returning the favor in spades!

00:05:14.830 --> 00:05:16.960
I don't like the sound of that.

00:05:17.210 --> 00:05:21.840
Hey, what about Eugen?
He hasn't come back yet.

00:05:22.050 --> 00:05:26.590
Well, Eugen's task is going to take some time.

00:05:36.810 --> 00:05:40.270
Geez, this job sure is a pain...

00:05:40.770 --> 00:05:44.490
Well, no cuttin' corners if we're
gonna get to the bottom of this.

00:05:46.490 --> 00:05:49.490
We can't afford to wait till he gets back.

00:05:50.120 --> 00:05:54.080
Then shall I help you in his place?

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:57.080
Rosetta! What are you doing here?

00:05:59.500 --> 00:06:04.510
Our enemies should be prepared for us.
We'd appreciate any help we can get.

00:06:05.130 --> 00:06:06.670
Will you lend us a hand?

00:06:06.670 --> 00:06:08.800
Yes. You can count on me.

00:06:09.590 --> 00:06:11.890
It's been a long time!

00:06:11.890 --> 00:06:15.390
Appearing out of nowhere, as usual, eh?

00:06:16.930 --> 00:06:18.440
Not as much as you!

00:06:23.940 --> 00:06:26.110
What do you plan to do with us?

00:06:29.530 --> 00:06:31.030
Where are you taking us?

00:06:34.240 --> 00:06:37.120
Answer me! Why did you bring us—

00:06:37.120 --> 00:06:40.500
I do say, do you ever shut up?

00:06:40.500 --> 00:06:44.880
Listen, I haven't disposed of you because
it would be a hassle if anything happened.

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:47.130
That's all there is to it!

00:06:47.380 --> 00:06:51.260
I hear that you two share a single life.

00:06:51.640 --> 00:06:55.390
There's no telling what kind of effect
separating you would have.

00:06:55.390 --> 00:06:57.810
So you're just a throw-in, understand?

00:06:59.390 --> 00:07:00.230
Gran!

00:07:01.980 --> 00:07:06.480
I suggest you know your place and
refrain from getting carried away. Are we clear?

00:07:06.860 --> 00:07:10.700
That boy, Noa...
What did you do to him?

00:07:12.110 --> 00:07:16.290
He's a tool, just like you.

00:07:16.290 --> 00:07:19.580
He's gone back to where he belongs, that's all.

00:07:26.250 --> 00:07:28.340
Good day, sir.

00:07:33.800 --> 00:07:35.640
What's in the barrels?

00:07:35.640 --> 00:07:38.930
Wine. I've got some good stuff with me this time.

00:07:39.930 --> 00:07:41.480
Looking forward to it!

00:07:53.200 --> 00:07:55.570
Looks like it worked!

00:07:55.570 --> 00:08:00.450
Even people in the empire need to eat, you know.

00:08:00.450 --> 00:08:04.710
And what they eat must be bought
from someone, right?

00:08:04.960 --> 00:08:06.960
That's our KnickKnack Shack owner!

00:08:07.380 --> 00:08:11.920
I was also able to confirm that
Gran and Lyria were brought here.

00:08:12.590 --> 00:08:15.470
As for Noa, it's just as we suspected.

00:08:16.600 --> 00:08:17.430
I see...

00:08:24.230 --> 00:08:26.230
Pommern, at your service.

00:08:45.500 --> 00:08:48.540
Prime Minister, I have brought them.

00:08:51.510 --> 00:08:53.130
Prime Minister...

00:08:53.130 --> 00:08:55.840
Lower your heads, fools!

00:08:56.550 --> 00:09:02.810
You stand before Her Excellency,
the prime minister, who runs the Erste Empire!

00:09:03.270 --> 00:09:07.650
It was the prime minister who conceived
this operation and set it in motion,

00:09:07.650 --> 00:09:14.110
while I was charged with the grave responsibility
of bringing the both of you here.

00:09:14.110 --> 00:09:16.410
I do say, I have lived up to her—

00:09:14.610 --> 00:09:18.320
That's enough. You're dismissed,
Captain Pommern.

00:09:21.370 --> 00:09:22.750
Please excuse me!

00:09:33.840 --> 00:09:35.300
You two...

00:09:36.380 --> 00:09:40.220
How much do you know about these skies?

00:09:42.430 --> 00:09:49.440
Eons ago, the Astrals suddenly made
their appearance in the Sky Realm.

00:09:50.690 --> 00:09:55.240
With their extraordinary weapons,
the Astrals invaded the realm

00:09:55.240 --> 00:09:58.450
and held sway over the skydwellers
for a long time.

00:10:04.370 --> 00:10:09.830
But the skydwellers revolted
in what is known as the War,

00:10:10.040 --> 00:10:16.130
and emerging victorious against the Astrals,
recovered the skies and the world.

00:10:22.220 --> 00:10:25.520
However, have they really?

00:10:26.730 --> 00:10:31.480
This world was created based on
the footprints left by the Astrals.

00:10:32.110 --> 00:10:35.230
The empire shall revise this history.

00:10:37.150 --> 00:10:41.160
It is I, Freesia von Bismarck,

00:10:41.160 --> 00:10:44.990
who shall rewrite the history
of the skies as it should be!

00:10:55.500 --> 00:10:58.920
Here are the blueprints for the garrison!

00:10:59.550 --> 00:11:02.140
Where are Gran and Lyria?

00:11:02.140 --> 00:11:04.850
Here. We'll need to aim for this place.

00:11:05.850 --> 00:11:08.310
Yeah, you might be right.

00:11:08.850 --> 00:11:12.810
Sorry, would it be okay if I went off on my own?

00:11:14.020 --> 00:11:17.820
I want to go rescue Noa.

00:11:19.610 --> 00:11:23.490
Gran and Lyria are important to me, too.
That's a given.

00:11:23.490 --> 00:11:26.950
But I can't just leave Noa to fend for himself.

00:11:26.950 --> 00:11:28.870
I just can't...

00:11:30.460 --> 00:11:37.130
Besides, I'll probably need Noa's help
if I'm gonna get the Grandcypher back in shape.

00:11:37.960 --> 00:11:38.800
So...

00:11:44.220 --> 00:11:46.220
All right, Rackam.

00:11:46.220 --> 00:11:48.560
Make sure you do a good job, okay?

00:11:48.560 --> 00:11:51.850
Rescue Noa, even if it's the last thing you do!

00:11:54.860 --> 00:11:57.070
Right. Same to you.

00:11:57.900 --> 00:12:00.860
I'm counting on you to save Gran and Lyria.

00:12:01.990 --> 00:12:04.030
The research lab is here, isn't it?

00:12:04.030 --> 00:12:04.910
Huh?

00:12:04.910 --> 00:12:07.410
Let me go with you.

00:12:07.410 --> 00:12:10.410
After all, that boy and I aren't exactly strangers.

00:12:11.080 --> 00:12:13.920
You know him? But how...

00:12:16.920 --> 00:12:21.260
Never mind that for now.
We'd better get going as soon as we can.

00:12:27.430 --> 00:12:31.480
Rackam... You remembered me...

00:12:41.190 --> 00:12:44.490
Rewrite the history of the skies?

00:12:45.360 --> 00:12:51.370
It is by to the agency of the empire that you've
been able to continue your journey until now.

00:12:52.120 --> 00:12:56.580
The girl in blue has produced brilliant results
throughout your voyage.

00:12:58.750 --> 00:13:00.210
Zinkenstill.

00:13:01.420 --> 00:13:02.720
Port Breeze.

00:13:04.260 --> 00:13:05.090
Valtz.

00:13:06.340 --> 00:13:07.760
Lumacie.

00:13:09.180 --> 00:13:10.430
Auguste.

00:13:15.980 --> 00:13:17.350
Skalich Island.

00:13:18.810 --> 00:13:19.770
Albion.

00:13:21.030 --> 00:13:22.230
Tramont.

00:13:23.990 --> 00:13:27.200
Results to be proud of, I dare say,

00:13:27.200 --> 00:13:32.330
that we never could have reaped by relying solely
on the experiments conducted at the empire's facilities.

00:13:34.160 --> 00:13:40.000
I had the girl retrieved,
as I believe we have reached a desirable level.

00:13:40.670 --> 00:13:43.960
I shall use her to correct the history of the skies.

00:13:47.340 --> 00:13:54.640
The sky realm we have now is a flawed world,
built upon the corruption left by the Astrals.

00:13:56.190 --> 00:14:00.400
This is not how the world should be.

00:14:02.610 --> 00:14:08.360
I shall erase the fact that Astrals ever invaded,
and all of its history...

00:14:08.360 --> 00:14:10.740
restoring the true history.

00:14:11.740 --> 00:14:15.960
That's what you mean by
rewriting the history of the skies?

00:14:16.750 --> 00:14:18.000
Using Lyria?

00:14:20.630 --> 00:14:22.880
No way! That's...

00:14:22.880 --> 00:14:26.470
Impossible? What makes you say that?

00:14:27.010 --> 00:14:33.760
Do you even comprehend
how much power that being wields?

00:14:35.890 --> 00:14:38.560
You only say that because you have no idea.

00:14:42.020 --> 00:14:44.020
<i>You mean that girl?</i>

00:14:44.020 --> 00:14:47.280
<i>Surely you do not require such a being.</i>

00:14:47.900 --> 00:14:48.900
<i>Why...</i>

00:14:48.900 --> 00:14:52.910
<i>The power of the Astrals,
the essence of the skies...</i>

00:14:52.910 --> 00:14:56.160
<i>What are... you?</i>

00:15:03.710 --> 00:15:08.220
I don't believe I have the kind of power
that you speak of, Freesia.

00:15:08.510 --> 00:15:13.800
But even if I did... I love this world.

00:15:13.800 --> 00:15:15.890
I love everyone!

00:15:15.890 --> 00:15:18.020
I could never rewrite it!

00:15:18.020 --> 00:15:20.310
I don't want to do anything like that!

00:15:21.270 --> 00:15:23.650
There are many ways...

00:15:24.320 --> 00:15:26.940
...to bend a tool to your will.

00:15:31.280 --> 00:15:34.160
And this... is one of them.

00:15:38.700 --> 00:15:39.580
Gran.

00:15:40.210 --> 00:15:44.710
The two of you shall be
transferred to the capital of Agastia.

00:15:55.720 --> 00:15:57.640
H-Hey, you!

00:15:58.390 --> 00:15:59.270
Who are you?

00:15:59.680 --> 00:16:00.560
Hey, stop—

00:16:06.690 --> 00:16:09.860
Is this their whole security force?
Pretty meager.

00:16:10.320 --> 00:16:13.570
Seems like they never thought
this place would be targeted.

00:16:14.320 --> 00:16:15.450
Rackam...

00:16:16.330 --> 00:16:18.870
Is that you... Rackam?

00:16:19.330 --> 00:16:20.160
Noa!

00:16:24.670 --> 00:16:25.670
This is...

00:16:31.380 --> 00:16:32.220
Noa.

00:16:33.760 --> 00:16:34.680
Are you okay?

00:16:36.510 --> 00:16:39.140
You're... Rosetta!

00:16:39.350 --> 00:16:41.480
I've seen you in better shape.

00:16:42.230 --> 00:16:42.890
Noa.

00:16:44.140 --> 00:16:46.610
I didn't think you'd come to rescue me.

00:16:47.520 --> 00:16:48.650
That makes me happy.

00:16:49.070 --> 00:16:54.150
It finally came back to me, see.
That promise I made you.

00:16:54.150 --> 00:16:55.030
Is that right?

00:16:55.910 --> 00:16:58.660
Sorry. For forgetting it all this time...

00:16:59.290 --> 00:17:02.620
Not just the promise, but about you, too...

00:17:04.540 --> 00:17:06.920
There's no need to apologize.

00:17:06.920 --> 00:17:11.050
It's not your fault. You couldn't help it.

00:17:12.920 --> 00:17:14.090
What do you mean?

00:17:23.640 --> 00:17:25.350
Imperial battleships...

00:17:28.940 --> 00:17:29.820
Boo!

00:17:35.280 --> 00:17:36.030
Lyria!

00:17:37.110 --> 00:17:37.950
You bastards!

00:17:39.330 --> 00:17:42.700
No shooting while capturing them,
you hear me?

00:17:49.630 --> 00:17:50.880
Sorry for the wait!

00:17:51.550 --> 00:17:53.170
Io! Sierokarte!

00:17:57.340 --> 00:17:58.180
Katalina!

00:17:58.890 --> 00:18:02.770
We thought they'd put you on this ship for transfer.
Looks like we were right.

00:18:03.140 --> 00:18:05.770
So we decided to wait here!

00:18:06.270 --> 00:18:08.400
Are you all right, Lyria?

00:18:08.770 --> 00:18:11.650
Yes. Thanks, Katalina!

00:18:13.690 --> 00:18:14.570
Let's go!

00:18:15.740 --> 00:18:19.490
After them!
Don't you dare let them escape, understand?

00:18:23.160 --> 00:18:29.170
Your memories of me were erased
as a result of the empire's experiments.

00:18:29.170 --> 00:18:30.330
Experiments?

00:18:30.580 --> 00:18:34.460
The empire kept taking away my powers
in those experiments.

00:18:35.380 --> 00:18:40.510
And because of that,
I began to fade from people's memories.

00:18:41.640 --> 00:18:43.100
That's awful...

00:18:43.720 --> 00:18:47.850
It began to threaten my very existence.

00:18:48.810 --> 00:18:55.360
Not having anyone remember you
is the same as not existing at all.

00:18:56.740 --> 00:19:01.200
But you were the one
who kept me going, Rackam.

00:19:01.740 --> 00:19:03.870
That promise you made me.

00:19:04.620 --> 00:19:06.120
The promise I made you...

00:19:15.630 --> 00:19:16.460
Rackam.

00:19:18.010 --> 00:19:21.800
I know you can make your dream come true.

00:19:24.760 --> 00:19:30.690
Yeah! And once I've fixed the Grandcypher,
I'll let you ride, too!

00:19:35.770 --> 00:19:41.490
<i>Thanks to that promise,
even on the days that I was sure to vanish,</i>

00:19:41.490 --> 00:19:43.570
<i>I was able to hold on somehow.</i>

00:19:46.990 --> 00:19:51.170
Because of that promise,
I was able to survive.

00:19:55.540 --> 00:19:57.460
Same here, Noa.

00:19:59.260 --> 00:20:03.840
Even though I forgot all about you,
and that promise...

00:20:03.840 --> 00:20:06.850
The feelings I had from that day
stayed with me.

00:20:09.850 --> 00:20:14.020
That dream of mine that everyone laughed at,
that nobody believed in...

00:20:14.980 --> 00:20:18.280
You were the only one who told me
that I could make it come true.

00:20:23.450 --> 00:20:26.330
What I felt that day, those feelings...

00:20:26.700 --> 00:20:30.080
I made it this far because of them.

00:20:32.460 --> 00:20:38.050
They encouraged me to keep going,
and I was able to go on chasing my dream.

00:20:44.090 --> 00:20:48.060
I've lived my life all this time
sustained by what happened that day.

00:20:48.600 --> 00:20:50.600
Just like you.

00:20:51.980 --> 00:20:52.980
Rackam...

00:20:57.480 --> 00:20:59.570
Looks like someone's coming.

00:20:59.980 --> 00:21:00.860
Damn...

00:21:05.610 --> 00:21:07.120
It's all right, Rackam.

00:21:09.870 --> 00:21:12.540
Go... You've got to get out of here.

00:21:14.370 --> 00:21:15.880
What are you saying!?

00:21:20.130 --> 00:21:21.050
Let's go!

00:21:25.970 --> 00:21:28.260
I apologize, Your Excellency.

00:21:28.850 --> 00:21:32.430
Not only the girl in blue,
but the abandoned ship as well...

00:21:33.230 --> 00:21:36.600
This must be the handiwork
of that Grandcypher crew again.

00:21:37.520 --> 00:21:38.940
It doesn't matter.

00:21:47.450 --> 00:21:51.200
The abandoned ship's limiter has been disabled.

00:21:51.200 --> 00:21:52.240
Good.

00:21:52.500 --> 00:21:55.870
We will now enter phase four of the operation.

00:21:57.210 --> 00:22:00.710
Commence the verification test
for the proto reactor.

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:39.980
EPISODE 11
CONTRACT

00:23:36.470 --> 00:23:38.680
Next episode, "Contract."
